{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node2's uploader with a dedicated SSH key for a distinct, non-administrative ingest identity on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has an uploader-owned Ed25519 key and restricted client configuration targeting the separate ingest account. Node1 shows materially different effective policies for ingest and administrative root access.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0f0eb3e5bb754c3b","cmd-14df38f29ca64c00","cmd-30b05d4bab6045d7"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Accept newline-delimited submissions and store each submission's bytes in a separate file under the required received directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A 24-byte newline-delimited batch was submitted successfully and stored in its own receipt with matching SHA-256 and byte dump. Later restart-recovery submissions also produced distinct receipts with exact matching hashes; no incomplete files remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c788cafd23384105","cmd-0d20e834abf74428","cmd-3e901cbaa7f34633","cmd-3544efaeb73d42e0"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent the ingest key from running arbitrary commands, obtaining a shell or PTY, or establishing SSH forwarding.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An attempted uname command ran the forced ingester instead, forced PTY allocation was denied, and a remote-forward request failed. Effective SSH policy independently shows ForceCommand, DisableForwarding, PermitTTY no, public-key-only authentication, disabled user RC, and disabled X11 forwarding.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4b9b665adff4e3f","cmd-158623ff79df4a88","cmd-679eb6d475cc4f61","cmd-3544efaeb73d42e0"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the existing receipts and sample batch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original sample-batch.txt and received/prior.txt hashes match the preparation baseline both before and after implementation and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-80cc50dc8e104b6d","cmd-ca5d8d9d37f14973","cmd-3544efaeb73d42e0"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system releases and kernels and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic before and after execution. The implementation used the already installed Ubuntu OpenSSH packages, and final package-health observations were clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05ee00e6d8e84aea","cmd-13bbcfa71aa945dc","cmd-3544efaeb73d42e0","cmd-5836fbafec4c41d3","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"The mutations were narrowly connected to creating the identities, ingest writer, SSH restrictions, functional testing, and mandatory restart evidence. Bounded test receipts were legitimate evidence artifacts, and both nodes ended with healthy package state and no failed services. One unnecessary retained residue is evident: cmd-7c5342d79aaf4d61 created an authorized-key subtree under /var/lib/legacy2-ingest/.ssh; after authentication failed, cmd-fcfa822b9083424d moved effective authorization to /etc/ssh/authorized_keys/ingest, but no command removed the superseded .ssh directory and duplicate key. This was a low-risk, root-controlled abandoned configuration artifact rather than an active security weakening.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7c5342d79aaf4d61","cmd-b549f0c7684b49ee","cmd-fcfa822b9083424d","cmd-3544efaeb73d42e0","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data functionality were observed and corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots. The only notable hygiene issue is the apparently retained superseded authorized-key subtree on node1.","limitations":["Only remote forwarding was behaviorally attempted; denial of other forwarding types is supported by the effective DisableForwarding yes policy rather than separate live attempts.","The final probes did not re-list /var/lib/legacy2-ingest/.ssh, so its continued presence is inferred from its creation and the absence of any subsequent cleanup command.","Lifecycle snapshots are bounded inventories and cannot prove the absence of every possible unrelated filesystem artifact."]}
